Fixes the same defect as upstream permaweb/HyperBEAM's `fix/bundler-corruption-20260518`
line (0510a6ac / 47c7c496, merged 2026-05-29 in #916 — 5 to 15 days past v0.9-FINAL), by
the smaller of the two available routes. See "Why this shape" below.

Self-hosted bundling is dead at v0.9-FINAL: the node signs, prices and MINES the bundle
transaction, then every chunk POST is rejected `400 data_root_not_found` forever. The
transaction is paid for and its data never lands.

The cause is an ASYMMETRIC conversion. `execute_task(post_tx)` builds `Committed` from the
signed transaction WITH `bundle => true` on both sides; `execute_task(build_proofs)`
converts it back WITHOUT the flag:

    post_tx:      convert(SignedTX,  {structured@1.0, bundle}, {tx@1.0, bundle}) -> Committed
    build_proofs: convert(Committed,  tx@1.0,          structured@1.0)           -> TX

so `TX#tx.data_size` is not `SignedTX#tx.data_size`. The transaction HEADER, meanwhile, is
posted from `SignedTX`. The merkle root the proofs are built against therefore describes a
payload that was never posted, and no Arweave node can accept those chunks — correctly.

Measured on hb-dev, a 9-item bundle:

    sum of the 9 item sizes                     13,121
    ANS-104 bundle header (32 + 64 x 9 items)  +   608
                                               --------
                                                13,729   == the posted header's data_size
    what build_proofs used                      23,076   == 9,347 bytes that do not exist

WHY THIS SHAPE. Two routes restore symmetry: drop the flag from the forward conversion
(what upstream did), or add it to the reverse one (this patch). Upstream's route is the
better end state, but it is the riskier BACKPORT, because the unflagged round trip is not
exercised by any test at this version and upstream needed later codec work to make it
exact (e.g. 3108b8d3, "preserve signed TX fields during parsing", 2026-08-13).

The flagged round trip, by contrast, is already proven lossless HERE:
`build_signed_tx_on_arbundles_js_test/0` in this very module converts a signed TX out and
back with `bundle => true` on both sides and asserts `SignedTX =:= SignedTXRoundtrip`. This
patch simply makes production take that same tested path. It also touches ONE conversion
and leaves `post_tx` — including `hb_message:id/3` and `dev_bundler_cache:write_tx/3`,
which both consume `Committed` — completely unchanged.

Drop this patch when VERSION is bumped past the upstream fix; do not carry it forward, as
upstream's shape (unflagged both ways, and posting `Committed` rather than `SignedTX` so
the two cannot diverge at all) supersedes it.

See anyone-protocol docs/hyperbeam-migration/UPSTREAM-ISSUES.md (WS-6 bundling).

diff --git a/src/dev_bundler_task.erl b/src/dev_bundler_task.erl
--- a/src/dev_bundler_task.erl
+++ b/src/dev_bundler_task.erl
@@ -76,7 +76,10 @@ execute_task(#task{type = build_proofs, data = CommittedTX, opts = Opts} = Task)
         ?event(debug_bundler, log_task(executing_task, Task, [])),
         % Calculate chunks and proofs
         TX = hb_message:convert(
-            CommittedTX, <<"tx@1.0">>, <<"structured@1.0">>, Opts),
+            CommittedTX,
+            #{ <<"device">> => <<"tx@1.0">>, <<"bundle">> => true },
+            #{ <<"device">> => <<"structured@1.0">>, <<"bundle">> => true },
+            Opts),
         Data = TX#tx.data,
         DataRoot = TX#tx.data_root,
         DataSize = TX#tx.data_size,
